"Each provider has its block","tour.varsModel.text":"The block holds what that provider needs: its API key, and `DefaultModel`, the model to use when an element names none.","tour.varsOthers.title":"More than one provider","tour.varsOthers.text":"Any provider an agent may call needs its block. Ollama runs on your own server, so it has a URL and no API key.","tour.analysis.title":"Invoice Analysis Agent","tour.analysis.text":"`OpenAI` with `gpt-4o`. Extracting five typed fields has to be right, because the next two steps build on it. This step gets the capable model.","tour.urgency.title":"Urgency Classifier","tour.urgency.text":"`Anthropic` with `claude-haiku-4-5`. One of three words from a single number: a small, cheap model is more than enough.","tour.risk.title":"Supplier Risk Check","tour.risk.text":"`Ollama` with `llama3.2`. Supplier names must not leave the company, so this step runs on a local model.","tour.log.title":"Three steps, three providers","tour.log.text":"One process, no Java code: each agent chose its own provider and model, and the log shows all three results.","tour.cleared.title":"Take the override away","tour.cleared.text":"Provider and Model are now empty on the Urgency Classifier.","tour.fallback.title":"Back to the global default","tour.fallback.text":"With nothing set on the element, the call goes to {provider} with {model}: the default from variables.yaml.","about.rules":"The provider and model of an agent decide where its call goes, shown above the agent while it runs. They do not change the simulated answer.|The Invoice Analysis Agent fills the fields of its result class from the invoice text.|The Urgency Classifier compares the amount with the limits in its system message.|The Supplier Risk Check answers LOW for a name with a company form such as Ltd. or GmbH, HIGH for a single word or something unreadable, and MEDIUM otherwise.","ref.tools":"Callable Process Tools","ref.guardrails":"Output Guardrail","ref.temperature":"Model Settings",